\b 1. License Grant\b0\par
Sunshine Technologies grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable license to install and use UltrON (Local Machine software and connected RajAPI services) on the facility/plant for which it was licensed. You may not copy, resell, sub-license, or reverse-engineer this software.\par
\par
\b 2. What This Software Does\b0\par
UltrON polls your Modbus-connected devices (TCP/RS485), stores readings locally in SQLite, computes CPCB-format averages and quality codes (U/O/E/N), and pushes this data to Sunshine Technologies' central server (RajAPI) for fleet dashboards, AMC management, and OTA updates.\par
\par
\b 3. Data Collection & Privacy\b0\par
This software collects device readings, timestamps, computed averages, device configuration metadata, and basic operational logs, and transmits them to RajAPI over a secured connection. Your data is not sold to third parties. Full details are in the Data Privacy & Processing Addendum provided with your service agreement.\par
\par
\b 4. Compliance Disclaimer\b0\par
UltrON is a monitoring and reporting tool only. It does not certify, calibrate, or guarantee your instruments' accuracy, and Sunshine Technologies is not a Pollution Control Board or certifying authority. You remain solely responsible for instrument calibration, data accuracy, and all statutory filings with CPCB/SPCB or any regulator.\par
\par
\b 5. Updates & Service Continuity\b0\par
This software may receive automatic OTA updates. Continued access to RajAPI-connected features (fleet dashboard, reports, remote support) requires an active AMC/subscription; access may be locked if payment lapses and restored on renewal.\par
\par
\b 6. Limitation of Liability\b0\par
Sunshine Technologies is not liable for inaccurate readings caused by faulty or uncalibrated client instruments, outages beyond its control, or regulatory penalties arising from your compliance obligations. Total liability is limited as set out in your Service & Installation Agreement.\par
\par
\b 7. Governing Law\b0\par
This Agreement is governed by the laws of India.\par
